# Tasks: PARTIAL-DONE

Purpose:
  Define the partial completion model for tasks that cannot fully
  complete. Some tasks span multiple layers (backend, frontend, mobile)
  where one layer finishes while another is blocked. Declaring
  PARTIALLY_COMPLETED prevents the illusion of full completion when
  only part of the work is done.

Owns:
  Per-layer completion status
  PARTIALLY_COMPLETED declaration
  Partial completion state transition

PartialCompletion:

  definition: task where one or more layers are complete but others
              are blocked, not started, or partially done
  declaration: PARTIALLY_COMPLETED (terminal-adjacent, not terminal)

  status_levels:
    complete     — all work for this layer done and verified
    in_progress  — work started, partial progress
    blocked      — blocked by external dependency or decision
    not_started  — no work begun on this layer
    skipped      — layer intentionally not needed for this task

  Example:
    backend:  complete
    frontend: blocked
    mobile:   not_started

  rule: [PD1] PARTIALLY_COMPLETED MUST list every affected layer
        with an explicit status.

LayerCompletionModel:

  layers:
    - backend      (BE)
    - frontend     (FE)
    - mobile       (MD)
    - database     (DB)
    - api          (API)
    - infrastructure (DO)
    - devops       (CI/CD)
    - security     (SC)
    - documentation (DOCS)
    - quality      (QA)

  PerLayerStatus:
    layer_name:
      status: complete | in_progress | blocked | not_started | skipped
      blocker: <explicit reason if blocked>
      required_human_action: <what human needs to do if blocked>

  Example:
    backend:
      status: complete
    frontend:
      status: blocked
      blocker:
        type: DEPENDENCY
        ref: BE-API-SPEC-003
        description: backend API contract not yet finalized
      required_human_action:
        approve API contract @decision.api-contract-v2

StateTransition:

  full_completion:
    all layers complete + Done Proof achieved -> COMPLETED

  partial_completion:
    some layers complete, others blocked/not_started ->
    PARTIALLY_COMPLETED
    action: record per-layer status, declare blocker,
            keep task open

  recovery:
    blocker resolved -> resume at the blocked layer's state
    (does NOT restart completed layers)

  rule: [PD2] PARTIALLY_COMPLETED is NOT terminal — task remains active.
  rule: [PD3] COMPLETED requires ALL relevant layers complete.

WhenPartialApplies:

  triggers:
    - dependency on another team's deliverable
    - external API not yet available
    - environment not provisioned
    - human decision pending
    - security review blocking deployment layer
    - upstream architecture decision pending

  rule: [PD4] If a layer is blocked, the AI MUST declare the blocker
        with type and ref — "blocked" alone is insufficient.

DoneProofForPartial:

  definition: Done Proof for the completed layers only
  format: same template as DONE-PROOF.sdd but scoped per layer

  Example:
    TASK-1023 PARTIAL DONE PROOF

    backend:
      requirements:       ✓
      tests:              ✓
      architecture:       ✓
      review:             ✓
      documentation:     ✓
      status: COMPLETE

    frontend:
      requirements:       ✗
      tests:              ✗
      status: BLOCKED
      blocker:
        type: DEPENDENCY
        ref: API-CONTRACT-003
        description: backend API not finalized

Rules:

  [PD1] PARTIALLY_COMPLETED MUST declare per-layer status explicitly.
  [PD2] PARTIALLY_COMPLETED is NOT terminal — task stays active.
  [PD3] COMPLETED requires all relevant layers to be complete.
  [PD4] Blocked layers MUST declare type + ref + required_human_action.
  [PD5] Completed layers within a partial task MUST pass their Done Proof.
  [PD6] When blocker resolves, task resumes at blocked layer state.
  [PD7] AI MUST NOT hide incomplete work behind "completed" status.
  [PD8] PARTIALLY_COMPLETED MUST be recorded in execution trace and summary.

